<!--
    Status bar and notification icon for push notifications: the Meetifyy
    mark (the M with the Y inside it), as a flat white silhouette.

    Android draws only the alpha channel of a notification's small icon and
    tints it itself (white in the status bar, the brand blue from
    notificationAccent in the shade), so this is one shape with no colour
    and no background. A coloured or full-bleed icon renders as a white
    square, and the launcher icon cannot be used for the same reason.

    The name is a contract: the server's FCM payload names this drawable
    (backend/src/push/providers/fcm.provider.ts, android.notification.icon)
    and the manifest makes it the default for any notification that names
    none. Every app state uses it: the FCM SDK builds background and killed
    notifications from the payload, and the push plugin builds foreground
    ones (when enabled) from the same payload.

    Traced from res/drawable-nodpi/meetifyy_splash_logo.webp and fitted to
    20dp inside the 24dp box (the platform's 2dp small icon margin).
-->
